            0.146
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "We substitute the values of a and b in the equation "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "y = ax + b"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " to obtain y = 20x + 150."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 3,
          "bbox": [
            0.111,
            0.146,
            0.886,
            0.205
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Thus, y = 20x + 150 represents the linear relationship between y, the bill amount in Rupees, and x, the number of GB of the internet data used."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "index": 4,
          "bbox": [
            0.131,
            0.222,
            0.399,
            0.246
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Think and Reflect"
            }
          ],
          "level": 2
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 5,
          "bbox": [
            0.128,
            0.259,
            0.868,
            0.298
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Can you guess what the numbers 20 and 150 in the equation "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "y = 20x + 150"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " represent?"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "index": 6,
          "bbox": [
            0.374,
            0.329,
            0.622,
            0.357
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Exercise Set 2.5"
            }
          ],
          "level": 2
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 7,
          "bbox": [
            0.132,
            0.382,
            0.886,
            0.499
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "1. A learning platform charges a fixed monthly fee and an additional cost per digital learning module accessed. A student observes that when she accessed 10 modules, her bill was `400. When she accessed 14 modules, her bill was `500. If the monthly bill y depends on the number of modules accessed, x, according to the relation "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "y = a x + b ,"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " , find the values of a and b."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 8,
          "bbox": [
            0.131,
            0.499,
            0.886,
            0.614
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "2. A gym charges a fixed monthly fee and an additional cost per hour for using the badminton court. A student using the gym observed that when she used the badminton court for 10 hours, her bill was `800. When she used it for 15 hours, her bill was `1100. If the monthly bill y depends on the hours of the use of the badminton court, x, according to the relation "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "y = a x + b ,"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " find the values of a and b."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 9,
          "bbox": [
            0.132,
            0.614,
            0.886,
            0.71
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "3. Consider the relationship between temperature measured in degrees Celsius (°C) and degrees Fahrenheit (°F), which is given by "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "^{\\circ}C = a^{\\circ}F + b"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " . Find a and b, given that ice melts at 0 degrees Celsius and 32 degrees Fahrenheit, and water boils at 100 degrees Celsius and 212 degrees Fahrenheit."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 10,
          "bbox": [
            0.17,
            0.71,
            0.886,
            0.769
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "("
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Hint:",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " When °C = 0, °F = 32 and when "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "^{\\circ}C = 100,   ^{\\circ}F = 212"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " . Use this information to find a and b, and thus, the linear relationship between °C and °F.)"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "index": 11,
          "bbox": [
            0.114,
            0.779,
            0.641,
            0.801
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "2.6 Visualising linear relationships"
            }
          ],
          "level": 2
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 12,
          "bbox": [
            0.112,
            0.809,
            0.884,
            0.868
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "As we have seen in many examples in this chapter, a linear pattern or relationship can be expressed in the form of an equation "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "y = ax + b."
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " Now we shall learn to plot such an equation as a straight line."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 13,
          "bbox": [
            0.111,
            0.867,
            0.886,
            0.907
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "To plot a linear equation, we need to identify any two points on the line. For example, to plot y = 2x + 1, we may identify two points as follows:"
            }
          ]
        }
